# Light Assistant Button Controller Firmware

## Overview
The main firmware file [firmware.ino](mdc:hardware/firmware/firmware.ino) implements a 40-button controller with RGB LED feedback. This controller serves as the primary input device for the Light Assistant system.

## Key Features
- 40 RGB LED backlit buttons arranged in an 8x5 matrix
- Three button states: inactive, active, pressed
- Two analog potentiometers for continuous control
- Serial communication with host computer
- Configurable LED brightness levels
- Support for multiple simultaneous button presses

## Communication Protocol
### Host to Device Commands
- `Cxxx:rgb` - Set button color (xxx=button number, rgb=hex color)
- `Axxx:1/0` - Set button active state
- `Bii:aa` - Set brightness levels (ii=inactive hex, aa=active hex)
- `X` - Host connected signal

### Device to Host Messages
- `Pxxx` - Button press event (xxx=button number)
- `Rxxx` - Button release event
- `Vxx:yy` - Potentiometer value (xx=pot number, yy=hex value)

## Core Components
- Button Matrix: 8 columns × 5 rows
- WS2812B RGB LED strip
- Arduino-compatible microcontroller
- Two analog potentiometers
